  "notes": "The research states a causal relationship rather than a preference — the sample register is high *precisely because* his high nasal timbre needs to cut against it — so `melody.register` [74,98] is the load-bearing parameter in this file and everything else is arranged under it. Two other numbers come straight out of the text: `kick.lockTo808` is 1, because \"kick-and-sub in a fixed relationship\" is exactly what that switch means, and `glideProb` is 0 because the research says \"no glides\" outright. The bass is `mirror_kick` at 0.94 for the long sustained sub anchoring the raised sample; the held-note rhythm the engine offers saturates, so a root on each kick is the honest substitute. ⚠ The I–IV family at weight 2 is a REDUCTION of the researched I–IV–V, not a separate claim. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates this medium-high — the sub-idiom is documented in detail but Freeway's own tempo band is catalog-level.",
